  "strings": {
    "A PDF is split into pages automatically — each becomes its own slide.": {
      "ref": "templates/pages/docs.html:211"
    },
    "A demonstration report: every value on the screenshot is invented.": {
      "ref": "templates/pages/docs.html:191"
    },
    "A file from a model, or a generator that computes in the browser": {
      "ref": "templates/pages/docs.html:43"
    },
    "A generator is a trusted Python package that the platform runs not on itself but on the analyst's machine: the browser starts Python in WebAssembly, reads the chosen folder through the system file access and sends up only the result — a finished HTML and its data files. The source Excel workbooks never leave the computer.": {
      "ref": "templates/pages/docs.html:233"
    },
    "A presentation is a list of slides, and a slide can be a live report, a picture, a PDF or an HTML page. In show mode the arrows page through the slides and a report opens for real rather than as a screenshot — the numbers in the meeting are fresh.": {
      "ref": "templates/pages/docs.html:205"
    },
    "A published file": {
      "ref": "templates/pages/docs.html:496"
    },
    "A published report as its reader sees it": {
      "ref": "templates/pages/docs.html:190"
    },
    "A real screen of the platform. Screenshots in this guide are taken automatically (tools/docs_shots.py), so they never drift away from the interface.": {
      "ref": "templates/pages/docs.html:98"
    },
    "A report in an hour": {
      "ref": "templates/pages/docs.html:128"
    },
    "A report that rebuilds itself": {
      "ref": "templates/pages/docs.html:225"
    },
    "A report where the origin of every number is visible": {
      "ref": "templates/pages/docs.html:23"
    },
    "A single file": {
      "ref": "templates/pages/docs.html:492"
    },
    "A title and a description help colleagues find the report; publishing can wait until you have looked at the draft.": {
      "ref": "templates/pages/docs.html:175"
    },
    "Addresses and storage": {
      "ref": "templates/pages/docs.html:503"
    },
    "An Excel import goes through a preview with a diff: what exactly will change is visible before a version is written.": {
      "ref": "templates/pages/docs.html:352"
    },
    "An administrator uploads the bundle, the platform checks the manifest, the dependencies and the semantics — and only then does the version appear in the list. After that a report is created from the generator: a draft, a first run on a real folder, publication.": {
      "ref": "templates/pages/docs.html:298"
    },
    "An optional file next to the manifest describes what the report means: canonical tables, views, metrics with their formula, rules and a glossary. The platform validates it against empty typed tables at registration time, so a typo in a column name is an error for the author, not an empty answer for the user.": {
      "ref": "templates/pages/docs.html:362"
    },
    "An unknown top-level key is a registration error: a typo in a contract has to be visible at once, not a month later on somebody else's machine. Declared inputs are not documentation: the engine reads exactly the files that match, and the platform builds the lineage map out of them.": {
      "ref": "templates/pages/docs.html:270"
    },
    "Asking a report questions in plain language": {
      "ref": "templates/pages/docs.html:368"
    },
