    "Markdown and Mermaid include column profiles (top values).": {
      "ref": "templates/pages/data_sources.html:109"
    },
    "Models (Claude, ChatGPT, Gemini) are good at writing a single self-contained HTML file: all the CSS and JavaScript inside, no external links. What matters is giving them the structure of the data rather than a description of it: paste 5–10 rows of your own extract straight into the request.": {
      "ref": "templates/pages/docs.html:136"
    },
    "No generator-backed reports you can run.": {
      "ref": "templates/pages/data_sources.html:27"
    },
    "No source matches that filter.": {
      "ref": "templates/pages/data_sources.html:256"
    },
    "Not sure where to start — then don't start here: the {a}School{a_} takes the same ground step by step, with checks and tasks on the platform. This guide is the better companion once you already know what you are doing.": {
      "ref": "templates/pages/docs.html:110"
    },
    "Observed on the most recent run that recorded inputs": {
      "ref": "templates/pages/data_sources.html:263"
    },
    "One self-contained HTML with versions and access": {
      "ref": "templates/pages/docs.html:48"
    },
    "OnePage is where a report lives after it has been made: people open it, ask it questions in plain language, rebuild it every week — and at any moment it is visible {b}which folder, which file and which sheet{b_} a number came from. The source data does not travel to the server on the way: the calculation runs in the analyst's browser.": {
      "ref": "templates/pages/docs.html:25"
    },
    "Only names and descriptions travel into the request to the model — of tables, of columns, of metrics. Not one cell of your data crosses that boundary: the calculation runs in the browser or on the platform's own server, and the model works with definitions.": {
      "ref": "templates/pages/docs.html:374"
    },
